      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can refactor some parts of this function. The part that scans a bitset and shifts it can be done together in a function like (untested):\n\n```\ntemplate \u003csize_t N\u003e\nsize_t ScanForwardAndShiftBits(std::bitset\u003cN\u003e\u0026 bits) {\n    if (bits.none()) {\n        return N; // Or some other indicator that there are no bits.\n    }\n\n    constexpr std::bitset\u003cN\u003e wordMask(std::numeric_limits\u003cuint64_t\u003e::max());\n    size_t offset \u003d 0;\n    while ((bits \u0026 wordMask).to_ullong() \u003d\u003d 0) {\n        offset +\u003d kBitsPerWord;\n        bits \u003e\u003e\u003d kBitsPerWord;\n    }\n\n    size_t nextBit \u003d ScanForward((bits \u0026 wordMask).to_ullong());\n    bits \u003e\u003e\u003d nextBit;\n    return offset + nextBit;\n}\n```\n\nThen I think we can write this function using that helper:\n\n```\n// Bits are currently shifted to mOffset + mSize.\nmOffset +\u003d mSize;\n\nsize_t rangeStart \u003d ScanForwardAndShiftBits(mBits);\nif (rangeStart \u003d\u003d N) {\n    // Reached the end, no more ranges.\n    mOffset \u003d\u003d N;\n    mSize \u003d\u003d 0;\n    return;\n}\n\nmOffset +\u003d rangeStart;\nmBits \u003d ~mBits;\n\nsize_t rangeCount \u003d ScanForwardAndShiftBits(mBits);\nif (rangeCount \u003d\u003d N) {\n    // All bits until the end of the set are set.\n    rangeEnd \u003d N - mOffset;\n}\n\nmSize \u003d rangeCount;\nmBits \u003d ~mBits;\n```",
